---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import ResumeReading from '../components/ResumeReading.astro';
import { ACTS, BOOK_DESCRIPTION } from '../lib/book';
import '../styles/book.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="UNNATURAL" description={BOOK_DESCRIPTION} cinematic>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="book-page" id="main-content">
    <section class="opening" aria-labelledby="opening-title">
      <div>
        <p class="book-kicker">An online book · Philosophy for the rest of us</p>
        <h1 class="book-title" id="opening-title">Life doesn’t always make sense.<br /><em>Even when it should.</em></h1>
        <p class="book-lead">You can understand the parts and still be puzzled by the whole. Including the part doing the understanding.</p>
        <p class="opening__promise">A journey into what moves us, how we make sense of things, and what it means to be part of the world we’re trying to understand.</p>
        <div class="book-actions"><a class="book-button" href="/chapters/prologue">Begin the book →</a><a class="book-link" href="/explore">See what’s inside</a></div>
        <ResumeReading />
      </div>
      <section class="recognitions" aria-labelledby="recognition-heading">
        <h2 id="recognition-heading">Which of these feels familiar?</h2>
        <p class="book-small">Open one that catches you. More than one is allowed.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>I keep doing things I don’t really want to do.</summary>
          <div class="recognitions__body"><p>Your hand opens the phone. There was no particular plan to look at it. There is a plan to put it down, although apparently that belongs to a different department.</p><p>We tend to picture a person deciding, then acting. Watch one ordinary reach. How much of the decision can you actually find?</p><a class="book-link" href="/chapters/01-before-thought-there-is-want">Begin with wanting · Chapter 1 →</a></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Everything is getting done. I’m not sure what it’s all for.</summary>
          <div class="recognitions__body"><p>You make the meal, wash the cup, clear a space. Tomorrow, most of this will need doing again.</p><p>We give plenty of attention to getting somewhere. A life also consists of feeding things, keeping things going, and being there. What makes any of it worth doing?</p><a class="book-link" href="/chapters/03-love-growth-and-meaning">Begin with what matters · Chapter 3 →</a></div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>I try to work it all out. Life keeps interrupting.</summary>
          <div class="recognitions__body"><p>You sit down to decide what sort of life to live. The body would like lunch. It has submitted this proposal before.</p><p>A plan is a picture of living. Living includes the body, the room, the people, and whatever your picture left out. How do we think, act, and leave some room for that?</p><a class="book-link" href="/chapters/13-the-three-cycles">Begin with how we meet things · Chapter 13 →</a></div>
        </details>
      </section>
    </section>
    <section class="book-section" aria-labelledby="book-about">
      <p class="book-kicker">Why “unnatural”?</p>
      <h2 id="book-about">Nature has started<br />making plans.</h2>
      <div class="book-copy">
        <p>We are made of the same world as everything else. Somehow we also make pictures of it: a shopping list, an idea of who we are, a rule about who owns the land.</p>
        <p>Then those pictures get to work. The list becomes a meal. The rule becomes a fence. A description of yourself starts deciding what you will try.</p>
        <p>This book follows that curious arrangement from wanting, through the distinctions we make, into the lives and worlds we build. There is a great deal to wonder about before anyone needs a grand theory. We will probably attempt one anyway.</p>
        <p>No philosophy background needed. The chapters use ordinary examples, room for disagreement, and small experiments with the ideas themselves. It is a book in progress. So, with rather less paperwork, are we.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="book-section" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
      <h2 id="journey-title">One question opens another.</h2>
      <ol class="book-acts">{ACTS.map(act => <li><a class="book-act" href={`/acts/${act.key}`} style={`--act-color: ${act.color}`}><span class="book-act__num" aria-hidden="true">{act.roman}</span><div><h3>{act.name}</h3><p>{act.premise}</p><small>Enter Act {act.roman} →</small></div></a></li>)}</ol>
    </section>
    <section class="book-section">
      <h2>Put an idea within reach.</h2>
      <p>Notice a want before explaining it. Try a map that leaves something out. Follow a few marks on a screen until they have moved your hand. Each exercise starts with a particular question from the book.</p>
      <div class="book-actions"><a class="book-button" href="/chapters/prologue">Start reading →</a><a class="book-link" href="/practice">Try an idea →</a></div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .opening { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr; gap: var(--space-12); align-items: start; padding: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-12); }
  .opening .book-title { font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 5.5vw, 4.8rem); max-width: 15ch; }
  .opening em { color: var(--color-act-i); font-weight: inherit; }
  .opening .book-lead { max-width: 34ch; font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .opening__promise { max-width: 43ch; color: var(--color-ink-muted); font-size: var(--text-base); }
  .recognitions { padding-top: .25rem; }
  .recognitions h2 { font: 380 var(--text-xl)/1.3 var(--font-display); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .recognitions details { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule); margin: 0; }
  .recognitions > p { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .recognitions details:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule); }
  .recognitions summary { padding: var(--space-5) 0; font: 380 var(--text-xl)/1.35 var(--font-display); }
  .recognitions details[open] > summary { margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--color-act-ii); }
  .recognitions__body { padding-bottom: var(--space-6); font-size: var(--text-base); color: var(--color-ink-muted); }
  .recognitions__body p + p { margin-top: 1em; }
  .recognitions__body a { display: inline-block; font-size: var(--text-sm); margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) { .opening { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-8); padding-top: 0; } .opening .book-title { max-width: 17ch; } }
</style>
